<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<dataModel xmlns="http://xmlns.oracle.com/oxp/xmlp" version="2.1"
           defaultDataSourceRef="ApplicationDB_FSCM">
  <!--
    DMT_BENBENEFICIARY_RECON_DM — Contract v1 reconciliation data model for
    BenBeneficiary (design section 5, "BIP reconciliation report contract - v1").

    Returns the BASE tier for the BenBeneficiary HDL load: one row per migrated
    beneficiary designation that is positively confirmed in Fusion, with its real
    Fusion base-table id as FUSION_ID. The object loads via HDL under the discriminator
    PersonBenefitBalance (see DMT_BEN_BENFY_HDL_GEN_PKG — 'BeneficiaryBenefitBalance is
    NOT a valid discriminator; use PersonBenefitBalance'). The load records one row in
    HRC_INTEGRATION_KEY_MAP keyed by the SourceSystemId we wrote, whose SURROGATE_ID is
    the Fusion PersonBenefitBalance base-table id. This report reads that map row exactly
    the way the Workers and Salaries reports do, so it needs no direct grant on the
    Benefits (BEN_*) base tables — the map's SURROGATE_ID IS the base-table id.

    RECORD_KEY = the beneficiary's business key = the prefixed PERSON_NUMBER || '_BENBNFY',
    which is exactly the value written into PersonBenefitBalance.dat as SourceSystemId
    (see DMT_BEN_BENFY_HDL_GEN_PKG) and stamped on the BenBeneficiary TFM row as RECON_KEY
    (one key definition per object).

    Verified live 2026-09-16 via scripts/fusion_bip_query.py (cred fin_impl):
      HRC_INTEGRATION_KEY_MAP.OBJECT_NAME        = 'PersonBenefitBalance' (838 rows;
        10 owned by HRC_SQLLOADER — our HDL loads, e.g. SOURCE_SYSTEM_ID
        '67936DMTBNFY001_BENBNFY' / '67936DMTBNFY002_BENBNFY')
      HRC_INTEGRATION_KEY_MAP.SOURCE_SYSTEM_ID   == the SourceSystemId we wrote (ends _BENBNFY)
      HRC_INTEGRATION_KEY_MAP.SURROGATE_ID       == the Fusion PersonBenefitBalance id
        (e.g. 300000331552758) — a real base-table id.
    Running this exact SQL with :P_PREFIX='67936' returned two BASE/SUCCESS rows with
    real Fusion ids. The physical Benefits base table (BEN_*) is NOT visible to the FSCM
    BIP data source (0 BEN_ tables reachable), so — like Salaries — BASE-tier proof is the
    map row whose SURROGATE_ID is the base-table id.

    HDL per-record failures arrive in the HDL response (tagged [FUSION_ERROR] by
    RECONCILE_HDL before this report runs), so this report returns the BASE tier only; the
    BenBeneficiary reconciler (which fetches these rows via DMT_RECON_CONTRACT_PKG.FETCH_ROWS
    and applies them statically) promotes a BenBeneficiary TFM row to LOADED only from a
    BASE / SUCCESS / FUSION_ID-not-null row here.

    Six Contract v1 parameters; keyset pagination by RECORD_KEY (P_AFTER_KEY).
    P_LOAD_REQUEST_ID / P_IMPORT_ESS_ID do not survive into the base table for an HDL load,
    so BASE-tier matching is by the run prefix (P_PREFIX). LOAD_REQUEST_ID is echoed back
    unchanged for audit.
  -->
  <dataProperties>
    <property name="include_parameters" value="true"/>
    <property name="include_null_Element" value="true"/>
    <property name="include_rowsettag" value="false"/>
    <property name="xml_tag_case" value="upper"/>
  </dataProperties>
  <dataSets>
    <dataSet name="benbeneficiary_recon" type="complex">
      <sql dataSourceRef="ApplicationDB_FSCM"><![CDATA[
SELECT object_type, record_key, source_type, fusion_status,
       fusion_id, error_message, load_request_id
FROM (
    -- BASE tier: positive proof via the HDL integration key map. The load writes one
    -- HRC_INTEGRATION_KEY_MAP row per beneficiary (OBJECT_NAME='PersonBenefitBalance')
    -- whose SURROGATE_ID is the Fusion PersonBenefitBalance base-table id. One row per
    -- migrated beneficiary.
    SELECT 'BenBeneficiary'                 AS object_type,
           m.source_system_id              AS record_key,
           'BASE'                          AS source_type,
           'SUCCESS'                       AS fusion_status,
           MAX(m.surrogate_id)             AS fusion_id,
           CAST(NULL AS VARCHAR2(4000))    AS error_message,
           :P_LOAD_REQUEST_ID              AS load_request_id
    FROM   hrc_integration_key_map m
    WHERE  m.object_name = 'PersonBenefitBalance'
    AND    m.source_system_id LIKE :P_PREFIX || '%'
    AND    m.source_system_id LIKE '%\_BENBNFY' ESCAPE '\'
    AND    (:P_AFTER_KEY IS NULL OR m.source_system_id > :P_AFTER_KEY)
    GROUP BY m.source_system_id
    ORDER BY m.source_system_id
)
WHERE ROWNUM <= :P_CHUNK_SIZE
      ]]></sql>
    </dataSet>
  </dataSets>
  <output rootName="DATA_DS" uniqueRowName="false">
    <nodeList name="data-structure">
      <dataStructure tagName="DATA_DS">
        <group name="G_1" label="G_1" source="benbeneficiary_recon">
          <element name="OBJECT_TYPE"     value="OBJECT_TYPE"     dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="OBJECT_TYPE"/>
          <element name="RECORD_KEY"      value="RECORD_KEY"      dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="RECORD_KEY"/>
          <element name="SOURCE_TYPE"     value="SOURCE_TYPE"     dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="SOURCE_TYPE"/>
          <element name="FUSION_STATUS"   value="FUSION_STATUS"   dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="FUSION_STATUS"/>
          <element name="FUSION_ID"       value="FUSION_ID"       dataType="xsd:integer" tagName="FUSION_ID"/>
          <element name="ERROR_MESSAGE"   value="ERROR_MESSAGE"   dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="ERROR_MESSAGE"/>
          <element name="LOAD_REQUEST_ID" value="LOAD_REQUEST_ID" dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="LOAD_REQUEST_ID"/>
        </group>
      </dataStructure>
    </nodeList>
  </output>
  <eventTriggers/>
  <lexicals/>
  <parameters>
    <parameter name="P_RUN_ID" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_RUN_ID" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_LOAD_REQUEST_ID" dataType="character" rowPlacement="2"
               labelID="P_LOAD_REQUEST_ID" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_IMPORT_ESS_ID" dataType="character" rowPlacement="3"
               labelID="P_IMPORT_ESS_ID" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_PREFIX" dataType="character" rowPlacement="4"
               labelID="P_PREFIX" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_CHUNK_SIZE" dataType="integer" rowPlacement="5"
               labelID="P_CHUNK_SIZE" defaultValue="5000" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_AFTER_KEY" dataType="character" rowPlacement="6"
               labelID="P_AFTER_KEY" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
  </parameters>
  <valueSets/>
  <bursting/>
</dataModel>
